course: dictionary
lesson: 5783
title: Lying: resting or not telling the truth
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one. «A single fallen tree can be home to hundreds of species, so nature reserves often leave dead wood lying.» Here lying means resting flat somewhere, like the wood lying on the ground.
explain: «Truthful lips endure for ever, but a lying tongue lasts only a moment.» Here lying means not telling the truth. Check by swapping in your meaning: a tongue that is not telling the truth makes sense, but a tongue that is resting flat does not.
explain: Lying is also a form of two verbs. Lie, lay, lain, lying means to rest flat. Lie, lies, lied, lying means to say what is not true. Read the whole sentence to find out which one is meant.
fact: Lying can mean resting flat on something, as in «lying in bed».
fact: Lying can also mean saying something that you know is not true.
fact: A lying person is someone who tells lies.
fact: The past tense of lie (to rest flat) is lay, and the past form is lain.
fact: The past tense of lie (to tell an untruth) is lied.
exercise: «The dog was lying by the fire.» What does lying mean here? | Telling an untruth | *Resting flat | Shouting loudly | Hiding under a bed
exercise: «Truthful lips endure for ever, but a lying tongue lasts only a moment.» What does lying mean in this sentence? | Growing tall | *Saying what is not true | Shining brightly | Resting flat on the ground
exercise: Which word fits? Yesterday the cat ___ on the warm mat. | lied | lies | *lay | lying
test: «Coins were lying on the ground, so the maths puzzle asked us to count them.» What does lying mean here? | *Resting somewhere | Stacked high | Telling untruths | Floating in water
test: Ruth says, «Stop lying, I saw you take the biscuit.» What does lying mean? | Resting on a sofa | *Saying something that is not true | Glowing in the dark | Falling over
exam: Which sentence uses lying to mean not telling the truth? | "The dead wood was lying in the forest." | *"Stop lying; I know where you were." | "The books were lying on the table." | "She was lying down because she felt dizzy."
